{"title":"G32 SuperFast: Bike Ahead & Stoll Team Up Again for Ultralight 32″ Gravel Bike Project","link":"https://bikerumor.com/g32-superfast-bike-ahead-stoll-team-up-again-for-ultralight-32-gravel-bike-project/","date":1795120674000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_angled-1536x1024.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Stoll + Bike Ahead G32 Superfast ultralight carbon 32\" /></p>\n<p>Stoll &amp; Bike Ahead announced a 10th anniversary collaboration that will see them turn this G32 Superfast prototype into an ultralight aero carbon production gravel bike on 32″ wheels early next year.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Describing it as “<em>a purpose-developed 32-inch concept, born from Swiss bike engineering and German carbon expertise</em>“, the G32 isn’t meant to replace the traditional 700c Superfast (which the Germans continue to refer to as 28″). Instead, the 32” bike will go a different direction, optimized for the speed and rolling efficiency of the bigger wheels, especially for gravel racing and ultra-distance riding.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Bike Ahead Composites + Stoll Bikes 32″ anniversary collaboration</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete.jpg\"><img width=\"2100\" height=\"1400\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete.jpg\" alt=\"Bike Ahead The Frame Projekt 32&quot; prototype XC bike fitted with BiTurbo RS 32 ultralight carbon wheels\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete.jpg 2100w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Bike-Ahead-Project-32-The-Frame-prototype-32-inch-XC-hardtail_complete-720x480.jpg 720w\" /></a><figcaption>Bike Ahead’s Projekt 32″ prototype at 2025 Bespoked <i>(Photo/Cory Benson)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>We’ve known pretty much since we first saw 32″ wheels on race bikes that Stoll and Bike Ahead were going to be at the forefront. Bike Ahead’s XC <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/bike-aheads-projekt-32-prototype-shows-off-real-big-6-spoke-biturbo-32-carbon-wheels/\" target=\"_blank\">Projekt 32</a> hardtail prototype was one of the first 32″ mountain bikes I saw in person. It was fitted with their own ultralight 6-spoke BiTurbo RS 32″ carbon wheels, which Bike Ahead’s Christian Gemperlein explained to me are even more of a benefit in the jump from 29″ to 32″, than they were going from 26″ to 29″</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM.jpeg\"><img width=\"1073\" height=\"715\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM.jpeg\" alt=\"profile shot of the Stoll Bikes P32 race bike for eh Absa Cape Epic\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM.jpeg 1073w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screen-Shot-2026-03-17-at-10.14.55-AM-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a><figcaption>Felix Stehli’s Stoll Bikes P32 race bike for the Absa Cape Epic <i>(Photo/Stoll)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Then, Stoll’s <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/32-inch-bikes-make-their-world-stage-debut-at-the-absa-cape-epic/\" target=\"_blank\">P32 full-suspension prototype</a> was the first time these even-bigger wheels were ridden to a race win on the elite level at this past spring’s Cape Epic.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Stoll + Bike Ahead G32 Superfast carbon gravel bike</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany.jpg\" alt=\"Stoll + Bike Ahead G32 Superfast ultralight carbon 32&quot; fast gravel bike project: development team in Wurzburg, DE\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_collaboration-team-in-Wurzburg-Germany-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption><i>(Photos/Bike Ahead)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The two ultra-premium carbon bike makers have already worked together for a decade, developing the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/bike-aheads-the-superfast-6-8kg-carbon-gravel-bike-the-one-7-8kg-xc-dream-build/\" target=\"_blank\">original Superfast</a> ultralight, aero gravel bike just last year. And in fact, Stoll frames are also manufactured in Bike Ahead parent All Ahead Composites’ factory in Würzburg, Germany. But to celebrate 10 years of working together, the G32 will officially be their first collaborative bike.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>“Stoll Bikes contributes its extensive experience in the development of geometry, ride dynamics, and design. Bike Ahead complements the project with its expertise in composite engineering, carbon layup, and manufacturing.”</em></p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser.jpg\"><img width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser.jpg\" alt=\"Stoll + Bike Ahead G32 Superfast ultralight carbon 32&quot; fast gravel bike project: teaser\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_promo-teaser-720x480.jpg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The two explain that the G32 project has been developed from scratch, taking into consideration the benefits of the larger wheelsize, like boosted speed, but also 32’s limitations.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The new G32 Superfast will feature all-new geometry optimized for the larger wheels. It doesn’t hurt that Bike Ahead customizable geometry cockpits help refine the fit for a wide rider size range.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>And it features completely new frame shaping as well. This prototype shares a few angular tubing profiles with the 700c Superfast. But the frame layout is totally unique. It features an extended headtube and curved seattube more like Stoll’s 32″ mountain bike. Then, all-new dropped seatstays, tapering toptube, and aerofoil downtube more like many modern aero road bikes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Tech details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close.jpg\"><img width=\"2500\" height=\"1500\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close.jpg\" alt=\"Stoll + Bike Ahead G32 Superfast ultralight carbon 32&quot; fast gravel bike project: up close\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close.jpg 2500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close-2048x1229.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_up-close-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>ultralight aero carbon 32″ gravel race bike</li>\n\n\n\n<li>two frame standard sizes M (170-184cm tall cyclists) and L (182-195cm riders)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>custom cockpit sizing, tailor-made for each rider</li>\n\n\n\n<li>optional 0.3L internal frame storage</li>\n\n\n\n<li>optional mounting points for all types of adventure gear</li>\n\n\n\n<li>60mm (2.36″) max tire clearance (<em>presumably not quite enough for 2.4″ MTB tires</em>)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3>What’s next? G32 Availability in early 2027!</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now.jpg\" alt=\"Stoll + Bike Ahead G32 Superfast ultralight carbon 32&quot; fast gravel bike project: 10th anniversary collaboration\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Stoll-and-Bike-Ahead-G32-Superfast-ultralight-carbon-gravel-bike-project_pre-order-now-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Officially, this is all still just a concept bike. But this is said to be a rideable prototype. And clearly the two are working on making this real.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Stoll &amp; Bike Ahead say the start of production for the G32 Superfast will be March 2027, suggesting you might be able to ride one by the end of next spring. No word on pricing yet, but a limited number of bikes are available to pre-order now, from either Bike Ahead or Stoll.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://bike-ahead-composites.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Bike-Ahead-Composites.de</a></em> &amp; <em><a href=\"https://www.stoll-bikes.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stoll-bikes.com</a></em> </p>\n\n\n\n<p></p>","author":"Cory Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/g32-superfast-bike-ahead-stoll-team-up-again-for-ultralight-32-gravel-bike-project/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"5de419ff542de7e91076d9587aba7d53dd074442c6d826486840df9649bfa6a0","category":"Cycling"}